## 4. Database Schema Review

### Strengths
- **22 tables** with clear responsibilities and no obvious normalisation issues
- `user_id` on every table + RLS = proper multi-tenancy
- `jsonb` for bilingual fields is the right Postgres pattern
- `UNIQUE(user_id, date)` on `ai_usage` prevents duplicate daily counters
- Soft enums via `text` columns with comments documenting valid values

### Issues & Recommendations

| Issue | Table(s) | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| No indexes defined | All | Add indexes on `user_id`, `exam_id`, `section_id`, and any column used in WHERE clauses. Performance will degrade with data growth. |
| `study_sessions.plan_id` has no FK constraint | `study_sessions` | Add `REFERENCES daily_plans` or document why it's intentionally loose. |
| `ai_logs` is missing `provider` and `model` columns | `ai_logs` | The spec's §2 says to log `provider` and `model` on every AI call, but the actual schema in §9 omits them. |
| `answer_archive.source_session_id` has no FK | `answer_archive` | Should reference `study_sessions` or `interview_sessions` — currently untyped. |
| No `updated_at` triggers | Most tables | Add `updated_at` columns with auto-update triggers for audit trails. |
| `chapter_frequency` lacks `user_id` | `chapter_frequency` | If exams are user-scoped, frequency should be too — or confirm it's derived from user-owned exams only. |
| No soft-delete pattern | All | Consider `deleted_at` columns for data recovery, especially on user-created content. |

### Missing Tables

| What's Missing | Where It's Referenced |
|---|---|
| `flashcards` or flashcard storage | §8.6 mentions "Auto Flashcard Generator" but flashcards go to `question_bank` — this works but blurs the line between past paper questions and AI-generated flashcards. Consider a `source` column. |
| `weekly_reports` | §8.4 mentions weekly reports generated every Sunday. Where are they stored? |
| `notification_log` | No record of which notifications were sent/read. |

